{
  "out": "/tmp/photonz-playtest/rotate-a-tilted-layer-live-walk",
  "seed": "Turning a layer on its knob shows the turn live, on every move, whatever the layer already carries. At Next defaults with no flag changed, on a recording: a plain rectangle is turned over two seconds and the picture must change on at least four moves in five and land exactly where it was held; the same rectangle is tilted 30 degrees on Y and turned again the same way, its outline on the tilted card; it is moved, and the moving picture keeps its tilt; a title is tilted and turned; a rectangle with a Position key is turned; two rectangles are grouped, the group is turned, and then a piece inside the turned group is turned. Each turn says how many new pictures a second it drew. The user found the picture standing still under a turning knob on a tilted layer on 2026-10-12, and the walk found it standing still on a plain one too: the drag's floated picture had not been shown for a turn since June.",
